		"title": "A weak definition, waiting to be overridden",
		"kind": "object",
		"command": "ld -o prog a.o weak.o strong.o",
		"request": "weak.o defines `dual` with STB_WEAK (binding 2) in the top nibble of st_info; everything else about the symbol — its section, st_value, st_size — is exactly what a strong definition would carry",
		"request_hex": "",
		"response": "With strong.o also in the link, the strong `dual` wins: the call site is patched to the strong body's address and the program exits 66. Drop strong.o and the very same link uses the weak body and exits 11",
		"response_hex": "",
		"note": "The rule is a total order, not a race: strong beats weak no matter which object came first on the command line. Checking only `is the slot already filled` gives the right answer half the time.",
